e:18px;mso-line-height-alt:27px">
<span style=3D"word-break: break-word; font-size: 18px;">Britain has a down=
sizing problem. Younger generations want bigger, more affordable homes, and=
 in many cases, older people do want somewhere more manageable to live.</sp=
an></p><p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"margin:0;mso-line-height-alt:21px">&nbsp;</p=
><p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:27px">
<span style=3D"word-break: break-word; font-size: 18px;">I moved home two w=
eeks ago, into a property that was being =E2=80=9Cdownsized from=E2=80=9D. =
But it had taken the seller three transactions and almost two years (ten mo=
nths alone on our chain) for this to happen.&nbsp;</span></p><p dir=3D"ltr"=
 style=3D"margin:0;mso-line-height-alt:21px">&nbsp;</p><p dir=3D"ltr" style=
=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:27px">
<span style=3D"word-break: break-word; font-size: 18px;">The process reveal=
ed to me that there are many things wrong with how we buy and sell houses i=
n this country, including that you can get to exchange and pull out without=
 any real consequences. But <a href=3D"https://link.thetimes.com/click/4798=
8691.63351/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cudGhldGltZXMuY29tL21vbmV5L21vcnRnYWdlcy9hcnRpY2xl=
L2JyaXRhaW4tZG93bnNpemluZy1jN2wwYnp6a3Y/6a464fcf7d55e1fcfb02eb9cB29451e26" =
target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener" style=3D"text-decoration: underline; col=
or: #006699;">looking at our readers=E2=80=99 comments</a>, the biggest =E2=
=80=93 and most complained about =E2=80=93 hurdle in our housing market is =
stamp duty.</span>
</p><p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"margin:0;mso-line-height-alt:21px">&nbsp;</p><p=
 dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:27px"><sp=
an style=3D"word-break: break-word; font-size: 18px;">Of the tens of thousa=
nds it cost us to move house (including the deposit for our mortgage, solic=
itors=E2=80=99 fees, survey and removals), 30 per cent of that was stamp du=
ty.&nbsp;</span></p><p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"margin:0;mso-line-height-alt:21=
px">&nbsp;</p><p dir=3D"ltr"=20
style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:27px"><span style=3D"w=
ord-break: break-word; font-size: 18px;">For us, it was a cost we had to sw=
allow to get the home we wanted. But if you were a homeowner who had spent =
40 years building up equity, why would you subject yourself to such a punit=
ive tax when you arguably don=E2=80=99t really need to?</span></p><p dir=3D=
"ltr" style=3D"margin:0;mso-line-height-alt:21px">&nbsp;</p><p dir=3D"ltr" =
style=3D"margin:0;mso-line-height-alt:27px">
<span style=3D"word-break: break-word; font-size: 18px;">Younger generation=
s deserve a chance to build up equity in decent homes like their parents be=
fore them, but until there is an incentive for those generations to move, w=
e are going to struggle to break this gridlock. </span></p><p dir=3D"ltr" s=
tyle=3D"margin:0;mso-line-height-alt:21px">&nbsp;</p><p dir=3D"ltr" style=
=3D"margin:0;mso-line-height-alt:27px">
<span style=3D"word-break: break-word; font-size: 18px;">It=E2=80=99s easy =
to point the finger at baby boomers for =E2=80=9Choarding=E2=80=9D family h=
omes, but the penalty for =E2=80=9Crightsizing=E2=80=9D is steep. We cannot=
 expect them to take the financial hit out of some sense of skewed moral du=
ty.</span></p><p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"margin:0;mso-line-height-alt:21px">&n=
bsp;</p><p style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:27px">
<span style=3D"word-break: break-word; color: #000000; font-size: 18px;"><s=
